      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=79825195\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Low impact]** This PR appears safe to merge.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nThis test-only change checks for `is_opaque_constant_type` before defining opaque operators.\n- PyTorch compile tests skip when an opaque-object API is missing.\n\n`pggPL` explicitly intends to skip all cases in this module when the required API is absent.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Skip torch.compile tests when required P...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/b0cbed0e023c715c2275ffabab984f4fade33283) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_expert&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=code_reviews&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
